## Reviewer got wrong (not applied as suggested)
- ne-b 2 suggested wording, not the finding. "अवश्य मेटिँदैन" is still an absolute ("certainly does not erase"). The finding itself (small print was made an absolute cure-bar) was applied with "सधैं मेटिँदैन".
- ne-b 15 treats the zero-width spaces as Nepali debris to delete. They match the Korean source and the checker counts them. Not a Nepali-only defect.
- ne-a 21, ne-a 22, and ne-b 24 correctly describe Nepal's lakh grouping. They were not applied because R14 and the pinned "TWD 1.57M" test reject that form. Not a misreading of the amounts.
- ne-a 2 is not a misreading of the URL: G0340028 is the withholding-rate standards and flno=3 is article 3. It was not applied because the Korean source still contributes a 10 ("제10조") and the checker requires that digit. English and Korean call that same URL the business-tax act, which is the mislabel; the Nepali statute name was already the withholding standards.
